# Commercial S12.1 atomic attempt and unknown-session diagnosis

- Scope: pre-freeze review of concurrent controller entry and simulator
  negative-session coverage.
- Findings:
  - two controllers could both pass the attempt-marker check while creating
    separate backups;
  - the deterministic Control simulator accepted a fabricated session object.
- Corrections:
  - `deploy` and rollback-only `recover` acquire a non-blocking exclusive flock
    on the verified frozen controller inode before preflight/backup; no lock
    file or pre-backup filesystem mutation is needed;
  - callback trigger requires object identity in the registered session map and
    the simulator executes an explicit unknown-session rejection journey.
- Boundaries: no second runtime start, no provider expansion, no secret output,
  and the sole server attempt remains unused.
